    "BML is a Dutch-taught full-time three-year molecular programme integrating chemistry, biology and physics, with a strong chemistry focus; the brief English overview does not turn it into an English-taught degree. Current Dutch prospectus and programme API agree on identity. There is no formal route to invent.",
    "Common part minimum 144 = 120 compulsory taught + 3 conditional mathematics/statistics + 21 experimental thesis. Add 36 genuine open credits. B1 has 57 compulsory taught + 3 conditional; B2 has ten compulsory six-credit courses; B3 contains 3-credit reflection, 21-credit thesis and 36 open. The prospectus rounds the year-three halves; the precise handbook controls.",
    "MAT14803 is the required three-credit choice for Mathematics A preparation, not an official-order tie-break. Mathematics B entrants take MAT15303 Statistics 1. The Math A example has period-1 second-half MAT14803 before period-2 first-half MAT15103 Analysis and second-half MAT15203 Linear Algebra. It does not combine incompatible MAT12806. The current admissions page accepts suitable Mathematics A or B profiles; no B-only restriction invented.",
    "Programme thesis-group entry requires at least 102 prescribed credits including all 60 B1 and the supervising group’s introductory second-year course. YML80321 MK specifies all60 B1 +42 B2 compulsory, AK all other compulsory courses. This concrete example completes all123 taught prescribed credits first, including all60 B2. A Biochemistry project follows both BIC20306 and BIC20806, the two BIC second-year core courses, thereby satisfying the public group-specific introductory preparation without selecting a fictional route. The organisational guide/agreement resides in Brightspace; no hidden course or arbitrary additional credit requirement is invented.",
    "YML80321 is an individual experimental research project with objectives, hypothesis/model and plan; a reproducible/verifiable laboratory journal, report, presentation and discussion are required. Participating groups BIC/BIP/BNT/CLB/GEN/MIB/MOB/ORC/PCC/PPH. Performance50%, report35%, presentation10%, finaldiscussion5%; final discussion minimum5.50. Thesis topics vary; a medicine/materials project is not guaranteed.",
